<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-AK3-QA2-002>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-AK3-QA2-002" ;
  triage:title "No in-repo execution evidence for required curl-integration smoke scenario" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr's AK3-QA-2 (PR #746 @ 6e2afd3b) confirmed the sprint doc's required-validation item -- a real curl frame to the configured peer listener reaching canonical persistence and emitting exactly one ordinary nudge for loopback, same-IP, and cross-host input -- has a smoke harness in place (scripts/smoke/run_feature_smoke.py) but no execution artifact for commit 6e2afd3b exists under reports/smoke/ in the worktree. SUPERSEDED at AK3-QA-3 (c0bb0c64): AK.2 (22ba8f92, already merged forward into this branch) deleted HttpsListenerSet/ListenerSecurity/PinnedClientVerifier and the entire custom-TLS listener lifecycle -- a deliberate, plan-sanctioned deletion documented in sprint-AK2-delete-peer-worker.md ('AK.2 leaves no legacy transport lifecycle. AK.4 creates the minimal plain receiver.'), corroborated by sprint-AK4-direct-peer-http-no-retry.md line 101 ('AK.2 deletes the legacy HttpsListenerSet module. AK.4 builds the replacement PeerHttpListenerSet') and sprint-AK6-remove-legacy-peer-transport.md line 88. No peer listener exists anywhere under crates/atm-daemon/src on this branch to curl against -- the scenario this finding demands is now structurally unexecutable, not merely unexecuted. quality-mgr independently confirmed no HttpsListenerSet/PeerHttpListenerSet symbol exists in the worktree, and arch-qa's AK3-QA-3 review independently reached the same conclusion (PASS, merge_ready true). req-qa's AK3-QA-3 FAIL citation (ATM-QA-AK3-QA3-005, claiming AK.2's doc says 'Retain only HttpsListenerSet lifecycle') does not exist anywhere in sprint-AK2-delete-peer-worker.md (grepped for 'Retain' and 'HttpsListenerSet' -- zero matching text) and is rejected as unverifiable. This finding's original premise (harness exists, execution not yet committed) no longer matches current reality (target deleted by design); the requirement is deferred to AK.4, which owns the replacement PeerHttpListenerSet receiver and 'is the first sprint that may claim a complete production send/read/ACK/nudge chain' per AK3's own sprint doc. AK3's sprint-doc Required Validation text describing a still-curlable peer listener is stale relative to AK.2's already-finalized deletion plan -- tracked separately as ARCH-AK3-DOC-001 (minor, non-blocking, routed to the planning branch), not as an AK3 code defect." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ak" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "important" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
